<title>UK: Novorossiisk reopens after brief closure - shipper.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk reopens after brief closure - shipper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's main oil export port Novorossiisk in the Black Sea briefly suspended loading of tankers overnight due to a thunderstorm, but it reopened on Friday morning, a shipping inspector said.</p>
<p>Loadings were suspended at 1600 hrs local time on Thursday evening and resumed at 0300 hours on Friday morning.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
